From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: USA-RedDragon <USA-RedDragon@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 01:45:05 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] fix(turns): a failed or interrupted turn keeps the user's
 queued message

When a Claude account hit its weekly limit, the running turn failed and every message Jacob had sent during it ("Queued: Talaria reads this when the current turn ends") was answered with "Your request was not processed. Send it again if you still want me to carry it out." The queue itself was not lost: after the failed turn the TUI gateway drained the queued prompt into a new turn. That turn failed on the same limit, and the core failed-turn closer (agent/conversation_loop.py::_close_durable_failed_turn) closed it with the same boundary row, whose copy told the user, and the model reading that row as its own words, that the message was dropped. The message did stay in the model's context (the boundary is a separate assistant row, so alternation repair never merges it into the next message), but both readers were told to forget it.

Every failed-turn boundary (the core closer, the gateway closers in gateway/run_turn_persistence.py, gateway/session_results.close_discarded_turn) now reads "This turn stopped before it finished. Your message is kept; I read it with your next message." (with "Some actions may already have run; verify their effects." when a tool ran). The old "not processed, send it again" copy is kept only for a turn the user cancelled: interrupt() records whether the stop was a user cancel (Stop / prompt.cancel / Ctrl-C, or a bare user interrupt) in _turn_user_cancelled, which outlives the finalizer's clear_interrupt() and is reset once the turn is closed. A new message that interrupts the turn is not a cancel: the TUI busy-input interrupt mode now labels its stop "user sent a new message" instead of a bare user interrupt. Restart, shutdown, timeout and watchdog stops pass their own reason and keep the message too, and the gateway restart and shutdown notices no longer ask for a resend. untyped_failed_turn_display_kind still recognizes the old stored texts.

Two paths really did drop messages. A steer accepted during a turn that failed (retry exhaustion, a non-retryable provider error) stayed in the agent's steer buffer: the failure paths return before finalize_turn, so no pending_steer reached the host and the text was in no transcript. run_conversation now hands it back as result["pending_steer"], which the TUI and gateway already run as the next turn. abort_turn_on_interrupt (an interrupt during retry backoff) dropped the steer buffer for every interrupt; it now drops it only for a user cancel. And after a restart, reopen_session and the resume mount paths deactivated every never-drained queued prompt row (#125577), so a queued message the hub had accepted vanished. The row is now re-placed: the early row is deactivated (kept as history) and an unmarked copy is appended at the transcript end, an open user turn that the auto-continue retry or the user's next message reads.
